        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Flynn Estate Agents are delighted to bring `Beechfield` to the open market for sale. Tucked away conveniently between The Square and Quay Street in the heart of Skerries, this impressive and substantial four-bedroom (plus attic conversion) residence enjoys a wonderfully central yet private setting, with the many amenities of this popular seaside town right on its doorstep. Situated just a stone`s throw from the North Beach, the property enjoys an enviable coastal setting, with the beach renowned for its spectacular sunsets and panoramic views across Skerries Harbour and towards the Mourne Mountains. Offering generous and versatile accommodation arranged over three floors, Beechfield presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a spacious family home in one of Skerries` most sought-after locations.\n\nUpon entering, you`re welcomed by a spacious entrance hall, with the accommodation thoughtfully arranged throughout the property. The ground floor provides a generous living room, dining area and kitchen, along with a separate sitting room, bedroom and bathroom, with the added benefit of own-door access. The layout offers excellent flexibility for modern family living, with a number of well-proportioned reception and living spaces that can be adapted to suit a variety of needs.\n\nUpstairs, the property continues to offer generous accommodation, with a further selection of well-proportioned bedrooms and bathrooms arranged across the first floors. The upper levels provide excellent versatility, with ample space for family members, guests or those requiring dedicated home office or hobby space. A particularly special feature of the second floor attic conversion is the spectacular views enjoyed from the dormer windows, overlooking Skerries Harbour and extending towards the beach and coastline.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a private courtyard, providing a charming outdoor space to relax and enjoy. The courtyard enjoys both morning and afternoon sunshine, making it a particularly pleasant space throughout the day and ideal for outdoor dining or entertaining.\n\nBeechfield is ideally positioned between The Square and Quay Street, placing it within easy walking distance of Skerries town centre and the coast. The picturesque and historic seaside town of Skerries is a thriving and friendly community, offering an excellent selection of shops, boutiques, pubs and restaurants, as well as a sailing club, Rugby, GAA and Golf Clubs, all close by. The coastline is lined with beautiful sandy beaches, while the surrounding countryside is mature and picturesque, with lovely tree-lined roads. Skerries is also well serviced by both bus and rail, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. Rush, Lusk and Balbriggan are all within easy reach, while Dublin Airport and the M1 and M50 motorways are also conveniently accessible.\n\n"
      },
